# Default branch has protection enabled
# Platform: GitHub (SDLC::Repository assets)
# CTN: github_branch_protection
# Frameworks: KSI-CMT-VTD, KSI-SVC-VRI, NIST CM-3, CM-5

META
    esp_id `github-branch-protection-exists-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `github`
    criticality `high`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `SDLC::Repository`

    title `Default branch has a protection rule`
    description `Validates that the repositorys default branch has any branch protection rule configured. Without protection, contributors can force-push, delete the branch, or merge unreviewed commits, breaking the SDLC integrity boundary.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `github,sdlc,branch-protection,ksi-cmt-vtd,ksi-svc-vri,nist-cm-3,nist-cm-5`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-VTD,KSI:KSI-SVC-VRI,NIST-800-53:CM-3,NIST-800-53:CM-5`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-VTD,KSI-SVC-VRI`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `GitHub:scanset:sdlc-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Settings, Branches, Branch protection rules: create a rule that matches the default branch name. Recommend starting with "Require a pull request before merging" plus blocking force pushes and deletions.`

    component_id `comp-github-sdlc`

    impl_KSI_CMT_VTD `The default branch is a managed configuration whose mutation is gated by an explicit protection rule rather than implicit contributor trust. The CTN queries the protection endpoint at scan time; an HTTP 200 (rule exists) passes, an HTTP 404 ("Branch not protected") fails with a finding. The 403 plan-restricted case is flagged separately so audit can distinguish operator-fixable misconfiguration from a paid-tier dependency.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_VRI `Verifiable resource integrity for the SDLC default branch requires a control surface at the repo level. Branch protection is that surface; the policy asserts its presence as the prerequisite for any downstream check (PR review, signed commits, force-push blocking) to have meaningful enforcement.`

META_END

DEF
    # Default placeholder values, overridden per-asset by PolicySetSync
    # at bind time. The VARs are pattern-fillers consumed by the template
    # OBJECT below; on bind, PolicySetSync rewrites the SET body with one
    # OBJECT per bound asset, each carrying that asset's concrete
    # owner / repo / branch from inventory.assets.metadata.
    VAR owner string `_unbound_`
    VAR repo string `_unbound_`
    VAR branch string `_unbound_`

    # Bound assets - managed programmatically by PolicySetSync from
    # inventory.asset_policies (status = active). Do not hand-edit;
    # the SET body is the only mutable region of this file.
    SET github_repos union
        OBJECT repo_target
            owner VAR owner
            repo VAR repo
            branch VAR branch
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE protection_rule_present
        found boolean = true
        protection_exists boolean = true
        protection_plan_restricted boolean = false
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN github_branch_protection
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF protection_rule_present
            SET_REF github_repos
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
